From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GLSL: emit continue blocks with scoped statements as structured code

STEAMAC-B6/B7/B8/B9 (1.9.13 and 1.9.15, M1, macOS 15.3.1, appids 5401090 and
5037200): MoltenVK shader library compile failed, "expected ')'", at
`for (uint _135 = 0u; _135 < 8u; ..., if ((... in bounds ...)), {,
_18[_156].write(...), }, _135++)`. dxil-spirv places the per-iteration
image writes in the loop's continue construct; with robustImageAccess2 MSL
guards each OpImageWrite with its own `if (...) { ... }` scope, and
CompilerGLSL::emit_continue_block captures the continue block's statements
and comma-joins them into the for-loop increment, scopes included.

When a captured continue-block statement opens or closes a scope, mark the
continue block complex and recompile, so the loop takes the existing
structured form (for (;;) with the continue block inline), as do-while loops
already do when their continue block has side effects. Robustness guards
are kept; branchless continue blocks keep the for-loop form.

Regression: host/moltenvk/repro/sentry-b6-continue.sh <spirv-cross>: a valid
SPIR-V loop writing texel i in its continue block reproduces `expected ')'`
with robustImageAccess2 before; after, MSL 2.4 and 3.0 compile with and
without robustness and the GPU writes texels 0-7 = 0-7, 8-15 untouched.
sentry-msl.sh's reconstructed shaders still pass.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/spirv_glsl.cpp b/spirv_glsl.cpp
index c7343a0..2d9399c 100644
--- a/spirv_glsl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_glsl.cpp
@@ -17863,6 +17863,21 @@ string CompilerGLSL::emit_continue_block(uint32_t continue_block, bool follow_tr
 	// Restore old pointer.
 	redirect_statement = old;
 
+	// steamac: statements the backend synthesizes with their own scope (MSL robustImageAccess2
+	// guards an image write as `if (in bounds) { write }`; atomic CAS loops) cannot be
+	// comma-joined into a for-loop increment: STEAMAC-B6/B7/B8/B9 emitted
+	// `for (...; ...; x, if (...), {, write, }, i++)` and Metal reported `expected ')'`.
+	// Emit the continue block as structured code on the next pass instead.
+	for (auto &s : statements)
+	{
+		if (s == "{" || (!s.empty() && s.front() == '}'))
+		{
+			get<SPIRBlock>(continue_block).complex_continue = true;
+			force_recompile();
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+
 	// Somewhat ugly, strip off the last ';' since we use ',' instead.
 	// Ideally, we should select this behavior in statement().
 	for (auto &s : statements)
